@host = http://localhost:5137

###############################################################################
# Fluxo completo: criar workflow -> cadastrar nodes -> executar -> consultar
#
# Rode as requisicoes na ordem. Copie o "id" devolvido em cada passo para a
# variavel correspondente logo abaixo.
###############################################################################

### 1. Criar o Workflow
# @name criarWorkflow
POST {{host}}/api/workflows
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "name": "Consulta SRC_DEV"
}

### Copie o id devolvido acima para ca:
@workflowId = 00000000-0000-0000-0000-000000000000


###############################################################################
# 2. Cadastrar um node SQL
#
# connectionStringKey = NOME DA CHAVE em ConnectionStrings do appsettings.json,
# nao a connection string inteira. "SRC" resolve para o servidor 10.10.10.17.
#
# O executor monta: SELECT TOP 1 [campo1], [campo2] FROM [tabela]
# Portanto "table" e "fields" precisam existir no banco alvo.
###############################################################################

### 2a. Node SQL apontando para SRC
POST {{host}}/api/workflows/{{workflowId}}/nodes
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "name": "Ler cliente no SRC",
  "type": "Sql",
  "connectionStringKey": "SRC",
  "table": "CLIENTES",
  "fields": ["ID", "NOME"]
}

### 2b. Node SQL apontando para o proprio banco do workflow
POST {{host}}/api/workflows/{{workflowId}}/nodes
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "name": "Ler workflow local",
  "type": "Sql",
  "connectionStringKey": "DefaultConnection",
  "table": "Workflows",
  "fields": ["Id", "Name"]
}

### 2c. Node HTTP (o resultado do node anterior chega como input)
#
# ATENCAO: "method" e NUMERICO, diferente de "type" que aceita string.
# Em CreateNodeRequest so o campo Type tem [JsonStringEnumConverter];
# Method nao tem, entao "Post" e rejeitado com HTTP 400.
#   Get = 1 | Post = 2 | Put = 3 | Delete = 4 | Patch = 5
POST {{host}}/api/workflows/{{workflowId}}/nodes
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "name": "Notificar sistema externo",
  "type": "Http",
  "url": "https://httpbin.org/post",
  "method": 2,
  "headers": {
    "Content-Type": "application/json"
  },
  "body": "{\"origem\":\"workflow-mvp\"}"
}


###############################################################################
# 3. Executar e acompanhar
#
# O POST /execute apenas ENFILEIRA a execucao. Quem processa os nodes e o
# Worker (WorkFlowProject.Worker), que faz polling a cada 2 segundos.
# Ele precisa estar rodando, senao a execucao fica pendente para sempre.
###############################################################################

### 3a. Disparar a execucao
# @name executar
POST {{host}}/api/workflows/{{workflowId}}/execute

### Copie o id da execucao devolvido acima:
@executionId = 00000000-0000-0000-0000-000000000000

### 3b. Consultar o andamento (repita ate concluir)
GET {{host}}/api/workflows/{{workflowId}}/executions/{{executionId}}


###############################################################################
# 4. Consultas auxiliares
###############################################################################

### Listar workflows
GET {{host}}/api/workflows

### Listar nodes do workflow
GET {{host}}/api/workflows/{{workflowId}}/nodes
